   are not declared on this satellite in data_7.js. Do not treat it as part of the
   ratified vault. ***
   anchor      : HUB_ORG_UNIT   (kind: hub, origin: map.anchor)
   track       : unratified
   history     : (not declared in data_7.js)
   feeders     : 1 emitted of 1 (one per source view AND run)
   runs        : 1 -- opus_health_v2
   payload     : 3 attribute(s), NULL-PADDED TO THE SATELLITE
   grain       : ONE ROW PER HUB_ORG_UNIT_HK
   hashdiff    : SAT_ORG_UNIT_CONTACT_HASHDIFF (builder decision BD1), GUARDED against an all-null input (s5.5):
                 without the guard every all-null row hashes to ONE value and the
                 satellite collapses to one row, which looks like change detection.
   INTRA-RUN FAN-IN, 2 attribute/run pair(s) with more than one writer, of
   which 2 are genuinely ARBITRARY. WITHIN one run several source views
   write the same attribute and the map declares NO precedence among them,
   so max() picks arbitrarily -- BUT ONLY AMONG UNDISCRIMINATED WRITERS. A
   writer carrying a resolved `instance` or a declared `redundant_of` is
   SEPARATED, not competing: a nominee's name and a policyholder's name on
   one satellite are DIFFERENT ROWS. BOTH SCOPES are quoted below because a
   bare writer count overstates the arbitrariness -- on PARTY_FULL_NAME it
   overstates it nearly fivefold.
   DECLARED, NOT RESOLVED: choosing among same-run writers would invent an
   authority the map does not provide. NO CROSS-RUN DECISION REACHES THIS.
     EMAIL_ADDRESS                          opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
     LANDLINE_NUMBER                        opus_health_v2         3 writer(s), of which 3 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
   A load-time assertion in models/assertions/ counts the DISTINCT
   values the undiscriminated writers actually supply per key. Until it
   runs, whether they ever disagree is UNKNOWN, not zero.
*/

with feeders as (
    select
        md5(upper('HUB_ORG_UNIT|' || (HUB_ORG_UNIT_BK__BRANCH_CODE))) as HUB_ORG_UNIT_HK
        , REN_TELEPHONE1 as LANDLINE_NUMBER
        , FAX as FAX_NUMBER
        , ITC_EMAIL_ID as EMAIL_ADDRESS
        , 'BJAZ_BRANCH_MASTER' as RECORD_SOURCE
        , 'opus_health_v2' as SOURCE_RUN
        , current_timestamp() as LOAD_DATETIME
    from {{ ref('stage_branch_master') }}
    where (nullif(trim(BRANCH_CODE),'')) is not null
),

resolved as (
    select
        HUB_ORG_UNIT_HK,
        max(case when SOURCE_RUN = 'opus_health_v2' then LANDLINE_NUMBER end) as LANDLINE_NUMBER,
        max(case when SOURCE_RUN = 'opus_health_v2' then FAX_NUMBER end) as FAX_NUMBER,
        max(case when SOURCE_RUN = 'opus_health_v2' then EMAIL_ADDRESS end) as EMAIL_ADDRESS,
        min(RECORD_SOURCE) as RECORD_SOURCE,
        min(SOURCE_RUN) as SOURCE_RUN,
        min(LOAD_DATETIME) as LOAD_DATETIME
    from feeders
    group by HUB_ORG_UNIT_HK
),

hashed as (
    select
        *,
        case when LANDLINE_NUMBER is not null or FAX_NUMBER is not null or EMAIL_ADDRESS is not null
                     then md5(upper(coalesce(cast(LANDLINE_NUMBER as varchar), '') || '|' || coalesce(cast(FAX_NUMBER as varchar), '') || '|' || coalesce(cast(EMAIL_ADDRESS as varchar), '')))
                end as SAT_ORG_UNIT_CONTACT_HASHDIFF
    from resolved
)

select * from hashed
where HUB_ORG_UNIT_HK is not null
  and SAT_ORG_UNIT_CONTACT_HASHDIFF is not null
